  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="eacd1759-be63-5a58-b117-79d03237246c" activityNameId="8a6424fe-e826-525b-ad3d-4a6d4c3e5ad8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sinter, iron, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sinter, iron, at plant
The date was taken from the publication by the European Commission 2013 with the Best Available Techniques (BAT) for iron and steel production (Remus, 2013).\nSpecific input factors and specific emissions factors have been determined for sinter plants. These data show a significant number of sinter plants in Europe representing 91.13 million tonnes of sinter production in 2004. Other input data, which include water input and the input of compressed air, were collected from five sinter plants in Europe representing 52.6 million tonnes of sinter production in 1999. \n\nAir emissions are average values and relate to European plants after abatement for sinter production in the EU-25 in 2004.;
Synonyms: In UVEK2018 enthalten; 
UUID: 7a17b8ce-03d6-3f3c-843d-e55dca095dc0
Blending, mixing and sintering. Emissions are abated
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7a17b8ce-03d6-3f3c-843d-e55dca095dc0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
